title: Smooth boards
intro: Match-3 gems, falling blocks, bars, a gun's kick, lights and the camera's zoom and shake are now drawn between the game's steps too.
project: Match3 | Smooth Gems

chapter: Ten steps a second | Gems that glide
say: The game moves in steps, sixty a second, and the screen is drawn between them, so things glide on a fast screen. Until now a match-3 board's gems, a falling-block piece, a bar's trail and a gun's kick still moved once a step.
say: To show the difference on any screen, this script slows the game down to ten steps a second. Whatever still moved once a step would jump ten times a second.
write: Scripts/TenSteps.cs | smooth-boards/TenSteps.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/TenSteps.cs | TenSteps.cs
hidecode
scene: Level1
select: Board
set: MatchBoard.Seed = 1
create: Empty
rename: Ten Steps
add: TenSteps
deselect
play
wait: 1
say: Swap two gems.
gameclick: 0.9, 3.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0.9, 2.5
wait: 2.5
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Swaps = 1
explain: game | Drawn between steps | Even at ten steps a second, the gems slide across, shrink away and fall into the gaps smoothly: each frame draws them part way between the last two steps.
stop

chapter: Falling blocks | A piece that glides down
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Blocks
select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Size = 11
deselect
create: Falling Board
create: Empty
rename: Ten Steps
add: TenSteps
deselect
play
wait: 2.5
tap: Left
wait: 1
tap: Right
wait: 1.5
explain: game | Falling and sliding | The piece falls a row and slides a column in a single step, but it's drawn gliding there. Full rows shrink away and the rows above drop into place the same way.
stop
say: Bars, a first person gun's kick and flash, lights, the camera's zoom and shake, and every game's heads up display glide the same way at the normal sixty steps a second.
